      "quote": "A total of 15 articles on models for malaria control optimization were identified from the literature. The majority of modelling analyses focused on countries in Africa and in the Asia Pacific regions. The interventions most commonly found in the analyses were ITNs, IRS, SMC and improved clinical case management. The data sources were country specific for some of the studies, although all studies had to rely on non-country-specific data to complete the analysis. The administrative level of analysis was at both the national and subnational levels, with a few studies having only subnational data analysis. There was a significant number of studies that had a budget constraint. However, very few carried out resource allocation within their constrained budgets.",
